// REJECTS: Field 'position' should be specified only once
//
// classView fields are an UNORDERED repetition in the grammar -- any order, and the
// grammar alone would accept any number of each. "Only once" is imposed afterwards by the
// walker, with this named-field message.
//
// The pairing with neg-diagram-classview-missing-class.pure is the point: same construct,
// same layer, two different named diagnostics, neither of them derivable from the .g4. A
// parser generated from the grammar accepts a classView with two positions and silently
// keeps one of them -- whichever its field-assignment loop happened to write last.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::TwicePositioned
{
   classView v1
   {
      class: fixture::neg::Person;
      position: (1.0,2.0);
      position: (3.0,4.0);
      rectangle: (10.0,20.0);
   }
}
